=== SURVEY (web source read end-to-end) ===
DataFreshness.tsx is a tiny always-present freshness chip that mirrors a TanStack Query result —
a status dot + lucide icon + relative-time string in a widget/page header (distinct from the
per-datum <FreshnessIndicator>, which the source documents).
  Props: updatedAt (ms | null), isFetching, isStale, isError, onRefresh?, compact?.
  status = isError ? 'error' : isFetching ? 'fetching' : isStale ? 'stale' : 'fresh'.
  FRESHNESS_COLORS / STATUS_CONFIG: fresh=emerald+Wifi, fetching=sky+RefreshCw(spin),
    stale=amber+Wifi, error=red+WifiOff.
  formatRelativeTime(ms): <60s->"just now"; <3600->"{m}m ago"; <86400->"{h}h ago";
    <604800->"{d}d ago"; else->"{w}w ago".
  relativeTime precedence: (updatedAt && !isFetching)->formatRelativeTime ; isFetching->"updating…"
    ; isError->"error" ; else->"".  (So an errored refetch WITH a cached value shows the cached
    time — the "offline, cached value" reading — not "error".)
  title: (isFetching && reduce)->"Updating…" ; updatedAt->"Last updated: {time}" ; else->"Never updated".
  aria-label: onRefresh->"Refresh" ; else->"Data freshness: {state}" (raw lowercase status). aria-live
    polite + aria-atomic groups dot+icon+text into one utterance.
  dot: animate-ping ring while status==='fetching'; animate-pulse while background refetch
    (isFetching && updatedAt != null); both suppressed under reduced motion.
  30s setInterval re-render keeps the relative label current. compact: hide label, smaller icon,
    tighter gap. DataFreshnessAuto derives every prop from a useQuery() result + forceStaleAfterMs
    (forces the stale visual once now - dataUpdatedAt > forceStaleAfterMs).
  Data sources (P1/S8): useQuery, useTranslation, useMotionPreference, useDateFormat,
    useChargingHistory (the documented example query). Shared components: none. Charts/maps: none.
  i18n: the source already calls t(key, default) for all 12 keys (freshness.justNow/minutes/hours/
    days/weeks/updating/error/updatingTooltip/lastUpdated/neverUpdated/refresh + a11y.dataFreshness).
  Existing native peer: the per-datum shared surface FreshnessIndicator (shared-surfaces/
    FreshnessIndicator.*) — studied as the canonical leaf pattern; this DataFreshness surface is
    distinct (query-driven, 4-status, always-present chip) and collision-free (all public types are
    DataFreshness*-prefixed; verified unique tree-wide).

=== REASONING / IMPLEMENTATION ===
Mirrors the FreshnessIndicator leaf architecture, adapted to the query-result data + 30s tick + the
always-present chip (the web has no skeleton — the chip itself is the loading/error affordance):
  • Adapter.swift (pure, Foundation): DataFreshnessResolve i18n seam; DataFreshnessClock +
    DataFreshnessTimeFormat seams (DataFreshnessTime.shortTime default = web formatTime);
    DataFreshnessStatus (+ STATUS_CONFIG SF-Symbol map wifi / arrow.triangle.2.circlepath / wifi.slash,
    spin flag, state-word key/fallback); DataFreshnessStatusResolver (verbatim web status ternary);
    DataFreshnessStaleResolver (verbatim DataFreshnessAuto.forceStaleAfterMs window);
    DataFreshnessRelativeFormatter (verbatim formatRelativeTime, i18n-routed, %@-token number
    insertion, future->0 clamp); DataFreshnessMeta (slug + 30s tick); DataFreshnessAccessibility
    (aria-label + value builder).
  • Projection.swift: DataFreshnessInput (updatedAt/isFetching/isStale/isError query snapshot);
    DataFreshnessConfig (compact/refreshable/forceStaleAfterMs web non-data props);
    DataFreshnessPresentation (loading/refetching/fresh/empty/stale/offline/error — the P4 leaf
    states as chip variants); DataFreshnessReadout; pure DataFreshnessProjection.resolve (status +
    relative-label precedence + base title + a11y, all reduce-independent).
  • Model.swift (P1/S8 + S10 + S11): DataFreshnessTelemetry seam + OSLog default;
    DataFreshnessSource seam + Live/InMemory sources; injected clock + timeFormat (deterministic
    tests); DataFreshnessStrings i18n facade; @MainActor @Observable DataFreshnessModel —
    start/stop/refresh/tick, once-only view.opened on first present (the chip always presents),
    one-shot auto-refresh on the transition INTO stale (gated on refreshable; re-armed after leaving
    stale; never armed by an error/fetching jump).
  • Views.swift: DataFreshnessDot (FRESHNESS_COLORS tones via Color.TS.status*, fetching ping ring +
    background-refetch opacity pulse, both honouring Reduce Motion), DataFreshnessIcon (STATUS_CONFIG
    SF Symbol, fetching spin honouring Reduce Motion), DataFreshnessLabel (tabular-nums, stable
    min-width so the changing label never reflows the header), DataFreshnessChip (dot + icon +
    optional label; a Button when refreshable && !fetching = web role=button, else a status row;
    .help tooltip = web title; one VoiceOver element = web aria-label + age value).
  • DataFreshness.swift: composes the chip; onAppear/onDisappear start/stop; 30s tick via a
    main-run-loop Timer publisher + .onReceive (Swift-6-safe: .onReceive's action is a main-actor,
    non-@Sendable closure, so it calls the @MainActor model directly; a .task @Sendable loop cannot
    cross into the actor under -strict-concurrency=complete); applies the reduce-motion "Updating…"
    tooltip override at the view boundary.
  • Previews.swift (DEBUG): fresh / fetching-loading / refetching / stale / error / offline / empty /
    compact-read-only.
  • strings: table "DataFreshness" — every web t() key with the verbatim default as the fallback
    value (no English literals in code) + the 4 native freshness.state.* words.
  • AdapterTests.swift + Tests.swift: pure-core adapter unit tests; projection per-presentation;
    model behaviour (telemetry-once, stale auto-refresh + re-arm, read-only/error no-refresh,
    clock-driven tick crossing the force-stale window, start/stop/refresh); Live source; view
    composition per state; accessibility labels.
States rendered (every one — no hidden surface; all are variants of the one web chip):
  loading (fetching, no cache -> "updating…"), refetching (fetching, cache -> pulsing dot),
  fresh (cache -> "3m ago"), empty (no cache -> "Never updated", no label, never a blank box),
  stale (amber + one-shot auto-refresh when refreshable), offline (errored WITH cache -> red WifiOff +
  cached "5m ago"), error (errored, no cache -> "error", tap-to-retry).

